menu "DWM3001CDK Aliro reader"

config ALIRO_PROV_SEED_HEX
	string "Reader provisioning blob to seed at boot (hex, bench only)"
	default ""
	help
	  Hex encoding of an aliro_prov ("APRV") blob, as printed by the
	  `aliro export` console command on a board that has been commissioned
	  into Apple Home. Empty (the default) leaves the reader on its dev
	  identity.

	  This board cannot be commissioned itself: no Matter image fits the
	  nRF52833, so an Apple-issued credential can only be adopted from a
	  board that was. This build has no console input either (CONFIG_SHELL=n,
	  RTT is output-only), so the blob arrives as a build-time string rather
	  than an `aliro-import` command.

	  The blob carries the reader PRIVATE KEY in the clear. A build with this
	  set is a bench artifact: whoever holds the .hex holds the reader
	  identity, and can impersonate the lock. Never set it for anything you
	  would call deployed, and keep the value out of version control.

	  Seeding runs on every boot and overwrites whatever is in the settings
	  store, so the baked value always wins.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
